{"causes": ["The rapid expansion of the early Islamic empire necessitated the systematic preservation of the Prophet Muhammad's teachings and practices.", "The passing of the Prophet's Companions created an urgency among the Tabi‘in to record their direct narrations before they were lost.", "Abu Hurayrah's prolific narration of hadith provided a rich source of traditions that required dedicated compilation and documentation."], "effects": ["His *Sahifah* provided one of the earliest written collections of hadith, serving as a critical foundational text for subsequent scholars.", "His work contributed to the development of hadith sciences by demonstrating early methods of compilation, dictation, and transmission.", "The traditions preserved by Hammām ibn Munabbih were integrated into later canonical hadith collections, influencing Islamic law and theology for centuries."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "hammam-ibn-munabbih", "sourceName": "Hammām ibn Munabbih", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "sahifah-hammam-ibn-munabbih", "targetName": "Sahifah Hammam ibn Munabbih", "context": "Hammām ibn Munabbih is credited with compiling the *Sahifah Hammam ibn Munabbih*, one of the earliest known written collections of hadith."}, {"sourceSlug": "abu-hurayrah", "sourceName": "Abu Hurayrah", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "hammam-ibn-munabbih", "targetName": "Hammām ibn Munabbih", "context": "Abu Hurayrah, a prominent Companion, was the primary source from whom Hammām ibn Munabbih narrated and collected hadith for his *Sahifah*."}, {"sourceSlug": "hammam-ibn-munabbih", "sourceName": "Hammām ibn Munabbih", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "damascus", "targetName": "Damascus, Syria", "context": "Hammām ibn Munabbih resided and taught in Damascus, a significant intellectual center of the Umayyad Caliphate during his lifetime."}, {"sourceSlug": "hammam-ibn-munabbih", "sourceName": "Hammām ibn Munabbih", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "imam-ahmad-ibn-hanbal", "targetN